#!/usr/bin/python3
# WynlandOS - leaf, the package manager.
#
# WynlandOS runs Ubuntu's binaries as they are, so leaf installs Ubuntu's
# packages: it reads the archive's signed index (InRelease, checked with
# gpgv against Ubuntu's keyring), resolves dependencies, downloads the
# .debs, checks each one's SHA256 against the index, and unpacks them
# itself. What it installed it can list, verify and remove again.
#
#   leaf update                  fetch the package lists
#   leaf search WORD...          packages whose name or summary has WORD
#   leaf show PKG                about a package
#   leaf install PKG...          install, with what they depend on and
#                                recommend, as apt (--no-install-recommends:
#                                only the dependencies)
#   leaf remove PKG...           remove what leaf installed
#   leaf upgrade                 newer versions of installed packages
#   leaf list [--installed|--base]
#   leaf files PKG               the files of an installed package
#   leaf owner PATH              which installed package a file is from
#
# State: /etc/leaf/sources (where from), /var/lib/leaf/lists (the index),
# /var/lib/leaf/installed.json (what leaf put where), /var/lib/leaf/base
# (what came with the system image), /var/cache/leaf (downloaded .debs).
#
